When I ran this code, the simulation standard deviation was 0.078, the average OLS standard error was 0.071 and the bootstrap simulation standard deviation was 0.064. These numbers may differ when reran due to no random seed being set. You can see that the simulation standard deviation is much higher than the bootstrap simulation and is closer to the OLS standard error. The bootstrap sample is treating each observation as independent when they are not independent, which could lead to the larger difference we are seeing between the two of them. This also shows that randomly resampling individual observations does not adequately capture the dependence between the errors, while the simulation sd does as it captures the variability that results from the dependence.  

